<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Basis levels continue to rise.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Basis levels continue to rise.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Basis levels for hard red winter wheat continued to strengthen amid heavy mill demand and a lack of farmer selling, traders said Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;Whatever's left out there isn't for sale. The farmer's sold what he has to. He's ready for harvest and he doesn't need to sell,&quot; a south-central Kansas dealer said. &quot;The result is that basis is on fire.&quot;</p>
<p>One merchandiser in Wichita, Kansas, raised its bid by 10 cents per bushel to 50 cents over the KCBT July contract. A Hutchinson, Kansas, merchandiser propped its bid up eight cents to 35 over.  </p>
